---
import IllustrationFigure from "~/components/illustration-kit/IllustrationFigure.astro"
import Panel from "~/components/illustration-kit/Panel.astro"
import SvgFigure from "~/components/illustration-kit/SvgFigure.astro"
import { series, stroke } from "~/data/palette"
---

<IllustrationFigure
  name="ladder-paradox"
  lead="The lengths change between observers. So does the timing of the doors."
>
  <p class="text-base leading-normal">
    The ladder moves through the barn close to the speed of light. Both observers agree
    that the doors close, but not that they close at the same moment.
  </p>

  <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
    <Panel title="From the barn" accent="gold" class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-2">
      <SvgFigure
        name="ladder-barn-view"
        class="w-full max-w-md"
        viewBox="0 0 360 205"
        title="Barn's view: the short ladder fits and both doors close together"
        desc="A 10 metre blue ladder fits completely inside a 12 metre gold barn. Beneath it, the near-door and far-door closing events line up at the same point in time."
      >
        <g fill="currentColor" font-size="15">
          <text x="10" y="18" font-weight="700">Barn: 12 m</text>
          <rect x="10" y="30" width="340" height="34" fill={series.gold}
            fill-opacity="0.25" stroke={stroke} stroke-width="1.5" />
          <rect x="38" y="40" width="284" height="14" fill={series.blue} />
          <line x1="10" x2="10" y1="27" y2="67" stroke={series.red} stroke-width="5" />
          <line x1="350" x2="350" y1="27" y2="67" stroke={series.red} stroke-width="5" />
          <text x="10" y="87">Ladder: 10 m — wholly inside</text>
          <text x="10" y="115" font-weight="700">When the doors shut</text>
          <text x="10" y="145">Near</text>
          <text x="10" y="175">Far</text>
          <path d="M88 140 H344 M88 170 H344" stroke={stroke} stroke-width="1"
            stroke-opacity="0.35" fill="none" />
          <line x1="224" x2="224" y1="136" y2="174" stroke={series.red}
            stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="3 3" />
          <circle cx="224" cy="140" r="6" fill={series.red} />
          <circle cx="224" cy="170" r="6" fill={series.red} />
          <text x="224" y="131" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" font-weight="700">
            Same moment
          </text>
          <text x="88" y="197" font-size="13">Earlier</text>
          <text x="344" y="197" text-anchor="end" font-size="13">Later →</text>
        </g>
      </SvgFigure>
      <p class="text-base leading-normal">
        Both doors close together while the shortened ladder is entirely inside.
      </p>
    </Panel>

    <Panel title="From the ladder" accent="blue" class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-2">
      <SvgFigure
        name="ladder-ladder-view"
        class="w-full max-w-md"
        viewBox="0 0 360 205"
        title="Ladder's view: the barn is short but the far door closes first"
        desc="A 20 metre ladder is longer than the 6 metre barn in this frame. The separate door-closing timeline shows the far door closing earlier than the near door, so the two are never closed together at one moment."
      >
        <g fill="currentColor" font-size="15">
          <text x="10" y="18" font-weight="700">Ladder: 20 m</text>
          <rect x="10" y="27" width="340" height="14" fill={series.blue} />
          <text x="10" y="65" font-weight="700">Barn: 6 m</text>
          <rect x="10" y="74" width="102" height="18" fill={series.gold}
            fill-opacity="0.25" stroke={stroke} stroke-width="1.5" />
          <text x="10" y="115" font-weight="700">When the doors shut</text>
          <text x="10" y="145">Near</text>
          <text x="10" y="175">Far</text>
          <path d="M88 140 H344 M88 170 H344" stroke={stroke} stroke-width="1"
            stroke-opacity="0.35" fill="none" />
          <circle cx="304" cy="140" r="6" fill={series.red} />
          <circle cx="136" cy="170" r="6" fill={series.red} />
          <text x="88" y="197" font-size="13">Earlier</text>
          <text x="344" y="197" text-anchor="end" font-size="13">Later →</text>
        </g>
      </SvgFigure>
      <p class="text-base leading-normal">
        The far door shuts first, then opens before the front of the ladder reaches it.
        The near door shuts later, after the back has passed. There is no moment when
        both doors are shut around the ladder.
      </p>
    </Panel>
  </div>

  <Fragment slot="caption">
    The coloured bars compare lengths <strong>within</strong> each observer's frame;
    the dots below show the order of the same two door-closing events.
    The paradox disappears when we stop assuming everyone agrees what happens
    at the same time.
  </Fragment>
</IllustrationFigure>
